---
import Default from "../layouts/Default.astro";
---

<Default
  title="Architecture"
  subtitle="4 layers, 5 Go modules, strictly top-down. Enforced by Bazel package_group + visibility — a rogue import fails bazel build before it ever reaches the linter."
>
  <article class="md-body">
    <h2>The 4 layers</h2>
    <pre is:raw><code>internal/
├── kernel/        stdlib-only AND generic primitives
│                  errs, buffer, clock, ring
├── core/          domain interfaces + domain values
│                  codec, logger, logger/level
└── service/       concrete implementations
                   logger (+ encoder, sink/{console,file,syslog},
                             middleware/{multi,async,route,
                                         failover,sample,recover})
                   codec  (asn1, baseenc, cbor, csv, flatbuffers,
                           json, msgpack, ndjson, pem, tlv,
                           toml, xml, yaml)
pkg/
└── v1/            stable public API (type aliases + ergonomic helpers)
    ├── logger/    (+ ldflags-injected Version)
    ├── errs/      (read-only introspection: CodeOf, ReasonOf, …)
    └── codec/     (blank-imports all 13 packages → 18 Format names)</code></pre>

    <h2>Dependency direction</h2>
    <p>
      Strictly top-down. Each layer may import only from layers <em>below</em> it. The
      table below is the contract:
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Layer</th><th>Imports allowed</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>internal/kernel/**</code></td><td>stdlib only</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>internal/core/**</code></td><td>stdlib + <code>internal/kernel/*</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>internal/service/**</code></td><td>stdlib + kernel + core (+ vetted third-party codec libs)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>pkg/v1/**</code></td><td>stdlib + kernel + core + service</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Module layout</h2>
    <p>
      Five independent Go modules glued by a workspace file:
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Module path</th><th>Build with</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>github.com/kitsunium/sdk/internal/kernel</code></td>
          <td><code>cd internal/kernel &amp;&amp; GOWORK=off go build ./...</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>github.com/kitsunium/sdk/internal/core</code></td>
          <td><code>cd internal/core &amp;&amp; GOWORK=off go build ./...</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>github.com/kitsunium/sdk/internal/service</code></td>
          <td><code>cd internal/service &amp;&amp; GOWORK=off go build ./...</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>github.com/kitsunium/sdk/pkg/v1</code></td>
          <td><code>cd pkg/v1 &amp;&amp; GOWORK=off go build ./...</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>github.com/kitsunium/sdk</code> (umbrella)</td>
          <td><code>go build ./...</code> at workspace root</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      <code>replace</code> directives in each <code>go.mod</code> resolve intra-repo
      dependencies without published pseudo-versions; <code>go.work</code> at the repo
      root lets <code>go build ./...</code> work from the workspace root. Third-party
      deps live only in <code>internal/service/go.mod</code> (cbor, msgpack, toml, yaml).
    </p>

    <h2>Enforcement</h2>
    <p>
      The layer firewall is <strong>not</strong> a linter rule — it's a Bazel
      <code>package_group</code> + <code>visibility</code> wall (ADR 0004). A rogue
      import fails <code>bazel build</code> before the linter ever runs.
      <code>.golangci.yml</code> exists as a code-quality second opinion only.
    </p>
    <p>
      Validation queries:
    </p>
    <pre is:raw><code># kernel must have zero outgoing go_library edges
bazel query 'kind(&quot;go_library&quot;, deps(//internal/kernel/...)) except //internal/kernel/...'
# expected: empty result

bazel build //...                           # all targets pass
bazel test --config=race //...              # every *_test target green
bazel run //:gazelle                        # regenerates BUILD.bazel after import changes</code></pre>

    <h2>Conventions per layer</h2>
    <h3>kernel</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Import-only-stdlib. Kernel packages MAY import each other (e.g. <code>ring</code> imports <code>errs</code> for sentinels) but MUST NOT reach into <code>core/*</code> or <code>service/*</code>.</li>
      <li>No domain vocabulary in public APIs — no <code>User</code>, <code>Request</code>, <code>Log</code>. <code>Queue[T]</code>, <code>Recycler[T]</code>, <code>Clock</code>, <code>Error</code> all pass.</li>
      <li><code>// IFACE-PLUGIN:</code> marker on constructors returning an interface backed by an unexported struct (the swap-able-implementation pattern).</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>core</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Interface-first. Core packages expose interfaces + immutable value structs. Any method with a non-trivial body belongs in <code>internal/service/*</code>.</li>
      <li>Role-suffix on exported structs (ktn-linter <code>KTN-STRUCT-ROLE</code>): <code>AttrValue</code>, <code>RecordEvent</code>, <code>WrapParams</code>. Short aliases (<code>Attr = AttrValue</code>) re-exported at <code>pkg/v1/*</code>.</li>
      <li>Plug-in registries (codec): constructors carry <code>// IFACE-PLUGIN:</code> markers.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>service</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Concrete implementations of <code>core/*</code> contracts. Where actual I/O, formatting, locking, codec dispatch and error wrapping happen.</li>
      <li>Codec registration <strong>without</strong> <code>init()</code> — each codec exports <code is:raw>var Codec codec.Codec = codec.Register(&amp;xxxCodec{})</code>.</li>
      <li>Error wrapping: <code is:raw>errs.Wrap(cause, WrapParams{…})</code> when the cause is stdlib / third-party. The <code>WrapParams</code> fields are silently ignored when the cause is already an <code>*errs.Error</code> (origin wins).</li>
      <li>Function length: <code>KTN-FUNC-MAXLOC</code> caps every function at 50 lines.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>pkg/v1</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Public types are <strong>type aliases</strong> onto <code>internal/core/*</code> / <code>internal/kernel/*</code> — zero runtime cost; consumer and SDK share the type identity.</li>
      <li>Public functions are thin wrappers: validation + delegation. No business logic.</li>
      <li>No constructors for internal types — consumers introspect SDK errors via <code>pkg/v1/errs.*Of(err)</code> accessors, but cannot forge <code>*errs.Error</code> values.</li>
      <li><code>pkg/v1/codec</code> blank-imports all 13 service codec packages so <code>import _ &quot;.../pkg/v1/codec&quot;</code> activates the full registry (18 Format names).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>See also</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/adr/0001-sdk-go-multimodule-layout/">ADR 0001 — multi-module layout</a></li>
      <li><a href="/adr/0004-sdk-bazel-build-system/">ADR 0004 — Bazel 9 as the single build system</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Default>
